# {{ project_name }}

STM32 firmware, generated from [stm32-template](https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/stm32-template).

Board: **{{ board_label }}**

## First-time setup

```sh
./tools/bootstrap.sh
```

Clones the pinned third-party submodules this board needs. (Plain
`git submodule update --init` won't work here — a generated project has
`.gitmodules` but no git history, so there are no gitlinks for git to act on.)

## Build (target)

```sh
cmake --preset {{ board }}
cmake --build --preset {{ board }}
```

Output lands in `build/{{ board }}/{{ project_slug }}.elf` (plus `.bin`, `.hex`, `.map`).

## Build & run tests (host)

Requires `ruby` on PATH (CMock uses it to generate mocks).

```sh
cmake -S test -B build/host-test
cmake --build build/host-test
ctest --test-dir build/host-test
```

## Flash

```sh
openocd -f interface/stlink.cfg -f target/{{ openocd_target }}.cfg \
  -c "program build/{{ board }}/{{ project_slug }}.elf verify reset exit"
```

